    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d249-a1">

                <pb facs="0531" n="461" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg461"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 632.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Lowell to Lord Granville.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-09-06"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 6,
                        1883</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Lord</hi> I have the honor to acquaint you that I
                    have recently received from Mr. Frelinghuysen a dispatch inclosing a letter from
                    the Acting Secretary of the Treasury, forwarding a report on the subject of the
                    foot-and-mouth disease made by the United States Treasury Cattle Commissioners,
                    in which it is stated that the disease does not prevail among the cattle of the
                    American herds.</p>
                <p>In compliance with Mr. Frelinghuysen’s instructions to bring the substance of the
                    report to your lordship’s attention, I have the honor to inclose a copy of it
                    herewith.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>J. R. LOWELL.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
